How to fuzz (safe command templates)
Use a limited rate, small wordlist, and authenticated session (cookies). Examples below use ffuf and gobuster.
FFUF (fast, flexible):
ffuf -w /path/to/wordlist.txt -u "https://test.com/FUZZ" \
  -H "Cookie: SESSION=your_session_cookie_here" \
  -t 20 -c -mc 200,301,302,403 -o ffuf_results.json
GOBUSTER (directory fuzzing):
gobuster dir -u https://test.com/ -w /path/to/wordlist.txt \
  -t 20 -b 404 -a "Mozilla/5.0" -s "200,301,302,403" \
  -k -H "Cookie: SESSION=your_session_cookie_here"
Notes:
•	Replace SESSION header with the actual cookie name from your authenticated session.
•	Use -t/-threads small (10–30) to avoid overloading the server.
•	Only include status codes you care about (200, 301, 302, 403, 401).
•	Add -c in ffuf to colorize and -mc to filter by response codes.
