What to watch for (and how to triage)
•	200 OK with meaningful HTML/JSON → inspect body for content, forms, links.
•	301/302 redirects → follow them; redirects to admin/login pages are interesting.
•	403 Forbidden but with different body message → may indicate auth enforcement but a reachable endpoint. Note the distinction between 403 and 401.
•	401 Unauthorized → endpoint likely requires creds; record existence.
•	Large Content-Length (compared to 404) → often indicates a valid page.
•	Responses with Set-Cookie or session changes → may indicate app state changes.
•	JSON responses containing schema names, table names, or data → high interest (capture sample and redact PII).

